      "id": 1,
      "text": "Amherst began as a tiny settlement called Amherst Corners, founded by pioneer Jacob Shupe in 1811.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amherst%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village plat was recorded in 1836, and the name shifted from Amherstville to North Amherst before settling on Amherst in 1909.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amherst%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Situated just 2.5 miles south of Lake Erie, Amherst lies within the Greater Cleveland metropolitan area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amherst%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Amherst Historical Society, founded in 1973, was accredited in 1990 and preserves the town’s sandstone heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
